{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "unraid",
  "description": "A full collection from Unraid 7.2. Field names come from the generated GraphQL SDL in unraid/api (api/generated-schema.graphql), not from the published docs, which still show a root dockerContainers query that does not exist in the schema. Proves: the collection is split into several small documents so one field a given schema lacks cannot fail every other query; machineId becomes a real foreign id that IS allowed to drive merges; br0 survives interface filtering even though the API reports virtual=true, because on Unraid the bridge IS the primary interface, while lo (internal=true) and docker0 are dropped; os.uptime is a BOOT TIME ISO string rather than a duration and becomes firstSeenTS; PrefixedID values arrive as '1:<id>' and the prefix is stripped; a macvlan container on br0 with a real LAN address becomes its own asset with its published ports as services; a container on Docker's default NAT bridge is NOT imported, because 172.17.0.0/16 is the same range on every Docker host and importing it would merge unrelated containers across servers; a container on host networking is not imported because it shares the server's stack and could never merge with anything; and VMs are recorded on the server rather than emitted as assets, because the schema exposes no MAC, address, or libvirt XML for a guest. The container MAC also pins the LAA divergence: the id keeps 02:42:c0:a8:01:3d losslessly while the emitted interface carries 00:42:c0:a8:01:3d, because net.network_interface clears the locally administered bit that Docker sets on every MAC it generates.",
